From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:10:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Enable the Allwinner A733 DSU devfreq
 driver

The A733 DSU driver lets the L3 cache clock follow the CPU frequency
policies. Build it as a module, like the other devfreq drivers of a
cache interconnect. The module loads by the compatible of the dsu node.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the module built from
this option loads on the dsu node, registers its devfreq device, unloads
and loads again.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 0d1d5bb4af12..1ac0dd2f665f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -1684,6 +1684,7 @@ CONFIG_TI_SCI_PM_DOMAINS=y
 CONFIG_ARM_IMX_BUS_DEVFREQ=y
 CONFIG_ARM_IMX8M_DDRC_DEVFREQ=m
 CONFIG_ARM_MEDIATEK_CCI_DEVFREQ=m
+CONFIG_ARM_SUN60I_A733_DSU_DEVFREQ=m
 CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ_EVENT=y
 CONFIG_DEVFREQ_EVENT_ROCKCHIP_DFI=m
 CONFIG_EXTCON_PTN5150=m
